From a421ea88c22e43c686ddac3ddfb1419b790e855a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noctrex <35490284+noctrex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:19:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] src: print the block-17 state-move VERIFY offset with %lld
 and a long long cast (block 17)

Block 17's serialised state-move VERIFY in llama_context::state_seq_move
logs the first differing byte as "first at %zd" with an (ssize_t) cast
of the size_t offset.  ssize_t is a POSIX type: the MSVC/UCRT headers
that clang++ uses under the Windows HIP SDK never declare it, and
llama-context.cpp includes no header that would, so a Windows build of
the llama library stops at llama-context.cpp with

    error: use of undeclared identifier 'ssize_t'

(the r346 build of ggml and ggml-hip completes; the failure is the first
src/ target, [469/722] of the default ninja set).

Cast to (long long) and print with %lld instead: the value is a byte
offset that is never negative, and the (size_t)-1 'no difference'
sentinel keeps printing as -1.  Identical output everywhere else.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 2bdd675..57cdda0 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -7210,8 +7210,8 @@ bool llama_memory_seq_state_take(
             }
         }
         LLAMA_LOG_INFO("%s: VERIFY seq %d: %zu of %zu byte(s) differ (%zu in the %zu-byte cell metadata), "
-                "first at %zd; the source rows are %s\n",
-                __func__, (int) seq_id, n_diff, size, n_diff_meta, meta_size, (ssize_t) first,
+                "first at %lld; the source rows are %s\n",
+                __func__, (int) seq_id, n_diff, size, n_diff_meta, meta_size, (long long) first,
                 n_diff == 0 ? "FAITHFUL" : (n_diff == n_diff_meta ? "re-placed (metadata only)" : "NOT the source's state"));
 
         if (n_diff > n_diff_meta) {
-- 
2.56.1.windows.1

